.TH BOSWAS-SESSION 1 "November 2026" "Boswas OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boswas-session \- start the Boswas OS desktop session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-session
[\fICOMPOSITOR-OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-session
is the program
.BR greetd (1)
starts after a successful login. It
.IP \(bu 2
reads the login profile (\fI/etc/profile\fR, \fI~/.profile\fR),
.IP \(bu 2
sets the session's environment (\fBXDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=Boswas\fR, Wayland
for Qt, GTK, SDL and Firefox, the Boswas defaults for KDE applications),
.IP \(bu 2
starts
.BR boswas-compositor (1),
which starts the shell,
.IP \(bu 2
publishes the session to the user's systemd manager and D-Bus and starts
\fBboswas\-session.target\fR (and with it \fBgraphical\-session.target\fR:
the device session agent, portals, autostart entries; the shell itself is
the polkit authentication agent),
.IP \(bu 2
stops that target when the compositor exits.
.PP
Options are passed on to the compositor.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/wayland\-sessions/boswas.desktop
The session entry.
.TP
.I /etc/boswas/greetd.toml
The login configuration greetd reads on Boswas OS.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/boswas\-session.target
The session target.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas-compositor (1),
.BR boswas-shell (1),
.BR greetd (1)
